<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL- Trading quietens down after hours.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL- Trading quietens down after hours.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traders said it was quiet after the markets closed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Wackenhut Corp reported after hours third-quarter earnings of $0.21 per share compared with $0.16 a year ago. Papa John's International Inc reported third-quarter net income of $0.26 per share, up from $0.16 a year earlier.</p>
<p>The Nasdaq Composite Index fell almost 13 points to 1203 amid concerns about retail computer sales during the day while the Dow Jones rebounded, gaining 34 to about 6007.</p>
